Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6556f811-1e9f-45ea-9c71-a020d54f9c48"],

Cell["\<\
This entry realises the cutoff-slice induced geometry of the accelerating, \
rotating, dyonic AdS4 black hole of arXiv:2106.05571, section 3.1 -- the \
object from which the renormalised boundary stress tensor T_ij and electric \
current j^i are extracted. The bulk solution is \
Sol__4dL__Accelerating-black-hole__PD (sections 2.1-2.2); the boundary theory \
scaffold is Thr__3dL__Boundary-minimal-gauged (recycled from the Vasko corpus \
via CopyData; run that first if the entry is missing under this alias).

The paper trades the radial coordinate for z via 1/r = alpha cos theta + z, \
so that the conformal boundary H = 0 sits at z = 0. In the polynomialised \
chart of the bulk entry (cos theta = -x) this reads r = 1/(z - alpha x). The \
four-dimensional coordinates are then (t, x, phi, z) and the ADM \
decomposition ds^2 = N^2 dz^2 + h_ij(dx^i + N^i dz)(dx^j + N^j dz) has a \
single nonvanishing shift component N^x -- the slices are NOT a \
Fefferman-Graham foliation, and the shift terms in the extrinsic curvature \
are what makes this calculation different from the corpus template \
Sol__3dL__Induced-black-hole__FG.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a9c19b0c-ee21-4435-aaa5-b0439ec8d91f"],

Cell["\<\
METHOD (the reason this entry is written abstractly). The exact slice data \
are bivariate rationals in (z, x) with seven symbolic parameters; \
substituting them before computing curvature makes every component a \
10^3-leaf object and the extraction never returns. Instead the induced \
metric, lapse and shift are kept as ABSTRACT FUNCTIONS of (zc, x[]) through \
the entire Compute chain, exactly as the corpus Sol__4dL__Black-hole__FG \
keeps u, v, az abstract. The explicit series enter only at extraction time. \
This is the corpus lesson \"the boundary lives in the expansion, not in the \
exact slice\".\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b7138a1d-3f4c-4d7a-8ad4-2a442fd6d98f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "GetData", "[", "\"\<Curated/Thr__3dL__Boundary-minimal-gauged\>\"", 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"full", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "GetData", "[", "\"\<Sol__4dL__Accelerating-black-hole__PD\>\"", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Load", "@", "sol"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.996914833625409*^9, 3.996914835328022*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f77002be-9388-4981-8edb-4cdcf72fc6d2"],

