Cell["Boundary action density", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c52701ab-512c-4d2f-b7b0-2aca04f9b8c9"],

Cell["\<\
The Gibbons-Hawking term together with the counterterms, S_bdy = (1/16 pi G4) \
Integral sqrt(-h)(2K - 4 - R(h)), as a Laurent series in the cutoff. The \
determinant of the induced metric has a leading coefficient which is a \
PERFECT SQUARE, ((1 + a^2 alpha^2 x^4)/(l4 kappa))^2; factoring it out by \
hand and expanding the remaining (1 + v)^(1/2) as a rational series keeps \
everything rational (Mathematica will not recognise the square inside a Sqrt \
of a large rational on its own). What is stored is the integrand density -- \
the x integration happens in the four-dimensional entry, where it meets the \
bulk contribution.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f2830990-eb98-49f2-914c-d0e194ec766b"],

