Cell["\<\
The bulk on-shell action of the four-dimensional entry, evaluated between the \
horizon and the cutoff slice, plus the boundary density above. The bulk \
antiderivative comes from the rule osabulk; r is traded for the cutoff by r = \
1/(zc - alpha x).

The divergence structure is worth recording. The leading z^-3 pole cancels \
pointwise in x, as in the Fefferman-Graham case. The two subleading poles do \
NOT cancel pointwise -- but they integrate to zero over x in (-1, 1). That is \
the signature of the shifted slicing: the mismatch is a total x derivative, \
invisible once the compact spindle direction is integrated. In FG gauge there \
is no such term.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c0aefc23-a73c-45ba-ac01-557a631d2b33"],

